2
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Vampire Journals is a horror, fantasy, thriller film directed by Ted Nicolaou.

3
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
A 19th century vampire stalks a more powerful vampire lord in his
quest to gain revenge over the death of his mistress.

4
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:06,000
In his search for the vampire lord in Eastern Europe he kills many of his servants
and fellow vampires while cursing another to vampirism as well.

5
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Ash, played by Jonathon Morris.

6
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Zachary, played by David Gunn.

7
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Sofia, played by Kirsten Cerre.

8
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Iris, played by Starr Andreeff.

9
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Cassandra, played by Ilinca Goia.

10
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Vampire, played by Constantin Bărbulescu.

11
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Interview with the Vampire is a 1994 American gothic horror film directed by Neil Jordan and written by
Anne Rice, based on her 1976 novel of the same name, and starring Tom Cruise and Brad Pitt.

12
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
It focuses on Lestat (Cruise) and Louis (Pitt), beginning with
Louis' transformation into a vampire by Lestat in 1791.

13
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
The film chronicles their time together, and their turning of
young Claudia (Kirsten Dunst) into a vampire.

14
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
The narrative is framed by a modern-day interview, in which Louis tells
his story to a San Francisco reporter (Christian Slater).

15
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
The supporting cast features Antonio Banderas and Stephen Rea.

16
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
The film was released by Warner Bros.

17
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
on November 11, 1994 to generally positive reviews and was a commercial
success, grossing $223.7 million against a $60 million budget.

18
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
It received two Academy Award nominations for Best
Art Direction and Best Original Score.

19
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
Kirsten Dunst was additionally nominated for a Golden Globe for
Best Supporting Actress for her role in the film.

20
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
A stand-alone sequel, Queen of the Damned, was released in 2002, with Stuart
Townsend and Matthew Newton replacing Cruise and Banderas respectively.

21
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
The film explores themes of sword, vampire, impalement, severed, severed head.

22
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
The tone is dark and intense.
